Main content column
The left/main column begins with a small margin from the edge of the viewport.

It uses:
- A consistent left alignment.
- Full-width sections wherever possible.
- Small gaps between related sections.
- Slightly larger gaps between major report groups.
The cards are not randomly sized.

Their widths are based on their information density.

For example:
- The four summary cards have equal widths.
- Overall Farm Picture uses a three-part horizontal arrangement.
- Field-by-Field Assessment uses the full content width.
- Priority Findings and Strengths split into two columns.
- Water Conditions splits into two approximately equal sections.
- Collapsible sections span the entire main column.
- The final three cards use equal or near-equal widths.
Sidebar
The right sidebar has a fixed-looking narrow width.

Its cards are stacked vertically.

Each card is independent and has its own border and rounded corners.

The promotional image is much taller than the utility cards.
Spacing
The screenshot uses relatively tight spacing because it is an information-heavy report.

For a code implementation, a reasonable starting point is:
Element	Suggested spacing
Page outer padding	8–12px
Gap between summary cards	6–8px
Gap between major sections	8–12px
Card inner padding	10–14px
Gap between sidebar cards	8–10px
Table cell padding	5–7px
Heading-to-content gap	8–10px

These are implementation estimates based on the screenshot, not exact measured design specifications.

12. Typography and icon system
Typography
The interface uses a compact, modern sans-serif typeface.

A suitable implementation would use Inter, Manrope, or a similar clean sans-serif.

The text hierarchy is:
Element	Approximate size	Weight
Main toolbar metadata	9–11px	Medium
Main metric headings	11–13px	Medium
Metric values	22–27px	Bold
Main section headings	13–15px	Semibold
Summary paragraphs	10–12px	Regular
Table headings	9–10px	Semibold
Table values	9–10px	Regular
Collapsible section headings	11–12px	Medium
Sidebar headings	11–13px	Semibold
Sidebar text	9–11px	Regular
Technical metadata	9–10px	Regular

The exact screenshot is relatively compressed, but a real responsive implementation should not preserve tiny text at the expense of readability. Increase the typography as necessary for larger screens.
Icon system
The interface is highly icon-oriented.

Icons are used to make sections identifiable before the user reads their headings.

The icon families include:
- Leaf – farm health and vegetation.
- Heart – evidence coverage.
- Shield – confidence.
- Field/grid – assessed fields.
- Warning triangle – risks.
- Check circle – positive conditions.
- Water drop – water conditions.
- Weather symbol – climate exposure.
- Plant symbol – crop and rotation.
- Lightbulb – recommendations.
- Clock – scheduling and timestamps.
- Printer – printing.
- Download – exporting.
- Database – data sources.
- Clipboard – audit.
- Timeline – evidence history.
- Bar chart – seasonal review.
Icons should use consistent stroke weight and visual proportions.

